\fs36 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 How is RAG different from fine-tuning an LLM?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Fine-tuning means: You\'a0
\f2\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 retrain the model
\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \'a0on new data so it \'93learns\'94 that information permanently. 
\f0\fs26 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Fine-tuning means\'a0
\f3\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 changing the model itself
\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \'a0by training it on new examples.\

\f1\fs28 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \
RAG means: You\'a0
\f2\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 do not retrain the mode : 
