\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec5 \

\f1\b0\fs24 \strokec5 An embedding is a dense vector representation of text where geometric closeness approximates semantic relatedness. Mechanically, the text is tokenized, each token is looked up in an embedding matrix, a transformer encoder makes the token vectors context-aware, and pooling (mean, CLS, or last-token) produces one vector, usually L2-normalized.\

