\f1 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 An embedding is a dense vector representation of text where geometric closeness approximates semantic relatedness. Mechanically, the text is tokenized, each token is looked up in an embedding matrix, a transformer encoder makes the token vectors context-aware, and pooling .\
\ls17\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Closeness means something because the model is trained contrastively ,So similarity reflects what the training data paired together, not logical equivalence. That's why embeddings are weak at negation, exact IDs, and numbers, and why I pair them with BM25 and a reranker.\
\ls17\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 For metrics: on normalized vectors, cosine, dot product, and Euclidean give identical rankings, because squared L2 distance equals 2 minus 2 cosine. So I normalize at write time and use inner product. Absolute scores aren't portable across models because embedding spaces are anisotropic, so thresholds must be calibrated per model.\
\ls17\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 For model selection, I start from public leaderboards but decide on Recall@K on a golden set from my own corpus, then weigh input length, dimensions and storage (Matryoshka models allow truncation), latency, languages measured per language pair, data residency, and lock-in, since switching models means re-embedding everything. For jargon-heavy domains, I fine-tune with contrastive loss on query\'96passage pairs from logs or synthetic queries with hard negatives, or use a query-side adapter to avoid re-embedding.\
\ls17\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 The biggest production risk is mismatch: a different model, version, prefix, or preprocessing between ingestion and query produces garbage with no error. I prevent it with a single embedding service that owns all of that and stamps the model ID on every vector.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
