\f2\b \cf0 \strokec5 IVF (Inverted File Index) : 
\f11\b0 \cb9 \strokec5 a highly popular approximate nearest neighbor (ANN) indexing mechanism used in vector databases to accelerate similarity searches across high-dimensional datasets. Instead of comparing a query vector to every single vector in the database (brute-force search), IVF partitions the vector space to drastically restrict the search scope, trading off a fraction of accuracy for massive gains in query speed
\f2\b \cb1 \strokec5 \
It has 
\f1\b0 \strokec5 two main stages: training/indexing and querying.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls18\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\b \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Indexing Phase (Clustering) : 
\f11\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls19\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f15 \uc0\u8259 
\f11 	}
\f4\b \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Space Partitioning: 
\f11\b0 The database uses an algorithm\'97
\f4\b typically k-means
\f11\b0 \'97to group the raw vectors into a specified number of geometric clusters (k, often configured as nlist). Each cluster is represented by a central point called a centroid. \
\ls19\ilvl0
\f1 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f15 \uc0\u8259 
\f1 	}
\f10\b\fs32 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 I
\f4\fs24 \strokec5 nverted Mapping: 
\f11\b0 The "inverted" concept borrows from classic text search, where a keyword maps to a list of matching document IDs. In vector IVF, the centroid identifier maps to a list of vectors (or their IDs) assigned to that specific cluster.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
