\f2\b \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 TF-IDF : 
\f1\b0 \strokec5 A term matters if it is frequent 
\f5\i \strokec5 in this document
\f1\i0 \strokec5  (TF) and rare 
\f5\i \strokec5 across the corpus
\f1\i0 \strokec5  (IDF).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls23\ilvl0
\f11 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\b \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Term Frequency (TF):
\f11\b0  How often a query word appears in a document. If a word appears multiple times, the document is generally more relevant.\
\ls23\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\b \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Inverse Document Frequency (IDF):
\f11\b0  How common a query word is across all documents. Rare words (like "BM25") carry significantly more weight than common words (like "the" or "system").\
\ls23\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\b \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Document Length Normalization: 
\f11\b0 How long the document is compared to the average document length in the database. A short document containing your keyword twice is usually more relevant than a 500-page book containing your keyword twice.
\f1 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

