\cf0 \
	
\f10\b \strokec5 Example
\fs32 :
\f1\b0\fs24 \strokec5  Suppose there are 20 total relevant documents for a query in your database. If your top 10 results (K = 10) contain 5 of them, your 
\f9 \strokec5 Recall@10
\f1 \strokec5  is 5/20 = (0.25) (or 25%). High recall means the system isn't missing important information\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls27\ilvl0
\f9 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f10\b \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Precision@K
\f2 \strokec5  
\f1\b0 : measures what percentage of the items in your top 
\f10\b\fs32 \strokec5 K
\f1\b0\fs24 \strokec5  results are actually relevant.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 \strokec5 \
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f9\b0\fs32 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0         
\f10\b\fs24 Example
