\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec5 I treat embedding selection as an evaluation problem, not a leaderboard lookup.\
First, hard constraints filter candidates: data residency, license, required languages, and a max input length that covers my chunks. From the survivors, I shortlist three or four using public retrieval benchmarks in my languages. But I make the decision on my own golden set: real queries labeled at the span level, sliced by query type (policy questions, exact IDs, Arabic, jargon, OCR-noisy documents), searched against the full corpus with exact search, so I\'92m measuring the model and not ANN error. I report recall@50 and NDCG with confidence intervals, and I re-test the top two inside the real pipeline with BM25 and the reranker, because what matters is the marginal gain.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

